{"name":"Prison Jumpsuit","hex":"#fdaa48","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"prison","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place or institution where people are held against their will, in the US especially for long-term confinement, as of those convicted of serious crimes or otherwise considered undesirable by the government.","Confinement in prison (sense 1)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To imprison."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prison"},{"term":"jumpsuit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A one-piece item of clothing originally used by parachutists.","A similar item of clothing used for outdoor sports such as skiing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jumpsuit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prison uniform","blocks":[{"text":"A prison uniform or a jail uniform is a set of standardized clothing worn by prisoners. It usually includes visually distinct clothes worn to indicate the wearer is a prisoner, in clear distinction from civil clothing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Contemporary_orange-white_striped_prison_uniform.JPG/330px-Contemporary_orange-white_striped_prison_uniform.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prison_uniform"},{"title":"Prison","blocks":[{"text":"A prison, also known as a jail, gaol, penitentiary, detention center, correction center, correctional facility, or remand center, is a facility where people are imprisoned under the authority of the state, usually as punishment for various crimes. They may also be used to house those awaiting trial. Prisons serve two primary functions within the criminal-justice system: holding people charged with crimes while they await trial, and confining those who have pleaded guilty or been convicted to serve out their sentences."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Pentonvilleiso19.jpg/330px-Pentonvilleiso19.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prison"},{"title":"Jumpsuit","blocks":[{"text":"A jumpsuit is a one-piece garment with sleeves and legs and typically without integral coverings for feet, hands or head. The original jump suit is the functional one-piece garment used by parachutists."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Red_Jumpsuit_2017.jpg/330px-Red_Jumpsuit_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jumpsuit"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Modern_chain_gang.jpg/500px-Modern_chain_gang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Modern_chain_gang.jpg/500px-Modern_chain_gang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Inmates outfitted in common present-day prison uniforms (gray-white), US","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AModern_chain_gang.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Buchenwald_Prisoners_83718.jpg/500px-Buchenwald_Prisoners_83718.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Buchenwald_Prisoners_83718.jpg/1280px-Buchenwald_Prisoners_83718.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Buchenwald_Prisoners_83718.jpg/500px-Buchenwald_Prisoners_83718.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dutch Jews wearing vertically striped uniforms at the Mauthausen concentration camp during World War II.[3]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABuchenwald_Prisoners_83718.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki